nswer/id #uuid "46995870-fd5c-52bf-8d60-a3a53e6b049c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "F(s)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441962}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186441951} :answer-field/id #uuid "b42be66f-2f5e-5b5e-8bde-f1bb580ea2f4" :answer-field/key "field-6" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442014} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2202e53c-8362-54c1-a712-585510d9289a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441944} {:answer/id #uuid "244f06ac-0ae7-5008-8b27-bc7253233120" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{t}{e}^{-st}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441945} {:answer/id #uuid "3a91e5a1-a660-55f2-baab-40111b102a41" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{t}{e}^{-st}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441957} {:answer/id #uuid "c02bcd62-55f7-5751-8615-61871609fdcc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441984}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186441944} :answer-field/id #uuid "c1998247-feae-5761-8354-c898923b4ac3" :answer-field/key "field-4" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442017}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485} :question/id #uuid "72ddd4c8-8e72-5f66-b964-d1ec00d699bb" :question/math-academy-id "q-331053" :question/problem "Suppose we wish to find $$\n\\displaystyle L\\{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,dτ\\}\n$$ given $L\\{f(t)\\}=F(s)$ for $s>{s}_{0}.$ Select the correct options in the reasoning below.\n\nLet $A(t)$ be the anti-derivative of $f(t)$ such that ${A}^{′}(t)=f(t)$ and $A(0)=$  {{field-1}}. Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,dτ=A(τ)\\,{|}_{0}^{t}=A(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy definition of the Laplace transform, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,dτ\\}=L\\{{{field-2}}\\}={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}A(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's use integration by parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=A(t) & ⇒ & du={{field-3}} \\\\ dv={e}^{-st}\\,dt & ⇒ & v=-\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}A(t)\\,dt & =A(t)({{field-4}}){|}_{0}^{\\infty }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\left(-\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st}\\right){A}^{′}(t)\\,dt\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $-\\frac{1}{s}A(t){e}^{-st}{|}_{0}^{\\infty }=$ {{field-5}}, we have\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}A(t)\\,dt=\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}{A}^{′}(t)\\,dt.\n$$\n\nFinally, using that ${A}^{′}(t)=f(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}{A}^{′}(t)\\,dt & =\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}f(t)\\,dt \\\\  & ={{field-6}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let $A(t)$ be the anti-derivative of $f(t)$ such that ${A}^{′}(t)=f(t)$ and $A(0)=0.$ Then,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,dτ & =A(τ)\\,{|}_{0}^{t} \\\\  & =A(t)-A(0) \\\\  & =A(t).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy definition of the Laplace transform, we can write\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}L\\{{\\int }_{0}^{t}f(τ)\\,\\text{d}τ\\} & =L\\{A(t)\\}={\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}A(t)\\,\\text{d}t.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, let's use integration by parts:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=A(t) & \\,⇒\\, & du={A}^{′}(t)\\,dt \\\\ dv={e}^{-st}\\,dt & ⇒ & v=-\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}A(t)\\,dt & =A(t)\\left(-\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st}\\right)\\,{|}_{0}^{\\infty }-{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }\\left(-\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st}\\right){A}^{′}(t)\\,dt.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince $A(0)=0$ and $\\frac{1}{s}{e}^{-st}\\to 0$ as $t\\to \\infty ,$ we have $-\\frac{1}{s}A(t){e}^{-st}{|}_{0}^{\\infty }=0$ and\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}A(t)\\,dt=\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}{A}^{′}(t)\\,dt.\n$$\n\nFinally, using that ${A}^{′}(t)=f(t),$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}{A}^{′}(t)\\,dt & =\\frac{1}{s}{\\int }_{0}^{\\infty }{e}^{-st}f(t)\\,dt \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{s}\\cdot F(s) \\\\  & =\\frac{F(s)}{s}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186442021 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9b991022-71e3-511d-bc60-1c00da984bcb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "-{e}^{st}\\text{ }dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441976} {:answer/id #uuid "9be9cec4-a70c-5f29-bfdb-e851e013edfb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{e}^{-st}\\text{ }dt" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441977}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186441977} :answer-field/id #uuid "6a91cc8a-1893-57a4-ab18-b6701b21fd12" :answer-field/key "field-3" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442008} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b1e4ee7-a4a8-50f8-92de-c0996cee8aa8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "A(τ)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441958} {:answer/id #uuid "532e7f80-01d2-5382-ae88-9e86960b366d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "f(τ)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441965} {:answer/id #uuid "b36c98c0-0dd3-5858-8df0-92709709c63e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{A}^{′}(τ)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441981} {:answer/id #uuid "dffad1d5-37c4-5363-b5cc-756b4e6daca3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498} :answer/value "{f}^{′}(τ)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186441994}] :answer-field/correct {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186441958} :answer-field/id #uuid "6d135224-fa94-510a-b5c2-da161575c9f6" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045494} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186442009} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "06fc54b3-e12f-563f-ad7c-4dcf67f6e141" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/re